    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **69 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification requirement in the owner-create flow.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger alongside the existing `AUDIT` logger:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. In `addOwner(...)`, after the owner is saved and the audit events are emitted, enqueued the welcome notification carrying both the owner id and the memberId:\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome ownerId={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nIt fires only on the successful-create path (all validation/quota rejections return early before this point) and after `saveOwner`, so `owner.getId()` and the assigned `memberId` are both populated. The new `Cp57Tests` acceptance test passes, and no existing test regressed.",
